{"search_note":"I found no reliable 2024 evidence of revenge-driven war aims, annexation, or a manufactured external threat used to justify a new major military campaign.

I also found no strong evidence that Sisi was merely using Gaza for foreign prestige; the public record instead shows repeated ceasefire diplomacy and border restraint.

The clearest negative evidence is domestic: the state’s economic-crisis crackdown suggests motive discipline was weaker at home than in external security policy.","evidence":[{"title":"President El-Sisi and Jordan’s King Abdullah II Hold Talks in Amman","publisher":"Presidency of the Republic of Egypt","date":"2024-04-01","url":"https://www.presidency.eg/en/%D9%82%D8%B3%D9%85_%D8%A7%D9%84%D8%A3%D8%AE%D8%A8%D8%A7%D8%B1/%D8%A3%D8%AE%D8%A8%D8%A7%D8%B1_%D8%B1%D8%A6%D8%A7%D8%B3%D9%8A%D8%A9/new142024-2/","summary":"Sisi joined a call for an immediate ceasefire and warned that military action in Rafah would have grave consequences. This is a direct defensive-security framing rather than prestige or revenge.","question_ids":["2B.3","2B.1","1B.1"]},{"title":"President El-Sisi Meets the CIA Director","publisher":"Presidency of the Republic of Egypt","date":"2024-04-07","url":"https://www.presidency.eg/en/%D9%82%D8%B3%D9%85_%D8%A7%D9%84%D8%A3%D8%AE%D8%A8%D8%A7%D8%B1/%D8%A3%D8%AE%D8%A8%D8%A7%D8%B1_%D8%B1%D8%A6%D8%A7%D8%B3%D9%8A%D8%A9/news742024/","summary":"The meeting centered on ceasefire efforts, civilian protection, rejecting displacement, and preventing the conflict from widening. That is consistent with distinguishing defensive needs from escalation for its own sake.","question_ids":["2B.3","2B.1","1B.8"]},{"title":"President El-Sisi Speaks with US President Biden","publisher":"Presidency of the Republic of Egypt","date":"2024-04-29","url":"https://www.presidency.eg/en/%D9%82%D8%B3%D9%85_%D8%A7%D9%84%D8%A3%D8%AE%D8%A8%D8%A7%D8%B1/%D8%A3%D8%AE%D8%A8%D8%A7%D8%B1_%D8%B1%D8%A6%D8%A7%D8%B3%D9%8A%D8%A9/news2942024-3/","summary":"Sisi said Egypt was working to achieve calm, a ceasefire, and a hostage-prisoner exchange, and warned that escalation in Rafah would worsen the humanitarian crisis and regional security. That is explicit de-escalation, not manufactured threat inflation.","question_ids":["2B.3","2B.1","1B.8"]},{"title":"Egypt won’t accept security changes on Gaza border, foreign minister says","publisher":"Reuters via Yahoo","date":"2024-09-18","url":"https://www.yahoo.com/news/egypt-wont-accept-security-changes-125617669.html","summary":"Egypt refused changes to prewar Gaza-border security arrangements and rejected any military presence on the opposite side of the Rafah crossing. This is a defensive sovereignty claim, not an expansionist one.","question_ids":["2B.3","2B.2","1B.6"]},{"title":"Egypt rejects Israeli proposal to coordinate on Rafah crossing: Reuters","publisher":"Ahram Online reporting Reuters","date":"2024-05-17","url":"https://english.ahram.org.eg/NewsContentP/1/523774/Egypt/Egypt/Egypt-rejects-Israeli-proposal-to-coordinate-on-Ra.aspx","summary":"Egypt rejected Israeli coordination over Rafah and insisted the crossing should be managed by Palestinian authorities. The rationale is border and sovereignty protection, not prestige coercion.","question_ids":["2B.3","2B.2"]},{"title":"Egypt: Halt crackdown on people voicing concerns over economic crisis","publisher":"Amnesty International","date":"2024-05-13","url":"https://www.amnesty.org/en/latest/news/2024/05/egypt-halt-crackdown-on-people-voicing-concerns-over-economic-crisis/","summary":"Authorities intensified arrests of protesters, striking workers, and online critics over prices and economic discontent. That looks like regime-survival repression, not a clean separation of security from politics.","question_ids":["2B.3","1B.5"]},{"title":"Egypt: More than 100 arbitrarily detained over calls for anti-government protests","publisher":"Amnesty International","date":"2024-07-18","url":"https://www.amnesty.org/en/latest/news/2024/07/egypt-more-than-100-arbitrarily-detained-over-calls-for-anti-government-protests/","summary":"Security forces arrested 119 people after online protest calls over price hikes and power cuts. That is strong evidence of domestic diversionary or survival-oriented coercion.","question_ids":["2B.3","1B.5"]}]}
